# NEXVARY CX Cloud — Installation Guide

**Bundle version:** ${BUNDLE_VERSION}
**Commit:** `${COMMIT_SHA}`
**Built:** ${BUILD_TIMESTAMP}

---

## Prerequisites

| Requirement | Minimum |
|-------------|---------|
| Operating system | Debian 13 (Trixie) or Ubuntu 24.04 LTS |
| RAM | 2 GB (4 GB recommended when building FreeSWITCH from source) |
| Disk | 20 GB (add 2 GB if building FreeSWITCH from source) |
| Root access | Required |
| Outbound internet | Required (package downloads, GitHub clone) |

## Application source revision

This bundle installs **exactly** commit `${COMMIT_SHA}`.
The installer reads the pinned SHA from `installer/RELEASE` and uses
`git fetch origin ${COMMIT_SHA_SHORT}… && git checkout FETCH_HEAD` — it never
installs the default branch tip. The installed SHA is recorded to
`/etc/nexvary/installed_revision` and verified before the installer exits.

## FreeSWITCH

FreeSWITCH is **installed by the installer** (`installer/lib/freeswitch.sh`).
No SignalWire account or token is required.

When `NX_SW_TOKEN` is not set the installer builds FreeSWITCH
v1.10.11 from the official GitHub source.
This takes **15–25 minutes** and requires ~2 GB of extra disk space.
Build dependencies are installed automatically.

If you have a SignalWire FOSS token, pass it to skip the source build:

```bash
sudo NX_SW_TOKEN=your_token bash INSTALL-NEXVARY.sh --domain=your.domain.com
```

## Existing Let's Encrypt certificate

If the host already has a valid Let's Encrypt certificate, the installer
reuses it automatically when `--domain=` matches the certificate's domain name.
No new certificate is requested and no Certbot flags are needed:

```bash
sudo bash INSTALL-NEXVARY.sh --domain=your.domain.com
```

The installer detects `/etc/letsencrypt/live/your.domain.com/fullchain.pem`,
writes both a port-80 redirect and a port-443 TLS server block, and sets
`APP_URL=https://your.domain.com` in the application `.env`.
Automatic renewal via certbot's systemd timer or cron job is preserved.

## Quick install

```bash
sudo bash INSTALL-NEXVARY.sh --domain=your.domain.com
```

The installer will:
1. Detect your OS and verify prerequisites
2. Install PHP 8.3, Node 20, PostgreSQL 16, Redis, Nginx
3. Build FreeSWITCH v1.10.11 from source (or use SignalWire repo if token set)
4. Fetch and deploy commit `${COMMIT_SHA}` from GitHub
5. Run database migrations
6. Configure Nginx (HTTP-only, or HTTPS if certificate detected)
7. Configure systemd services and queue workers
8. Print the setup wizard URL

## Upgrading an existing installation

Re-run the installer with the **new** bundle, passing the SHA that is currently
installed as `--upgrade-from`:

```bash
# Find the currently installed SHA:
cat /etc/nexvary/installed_revision

# Then run the new bundle's installer:
sudo bash INSTALL-NEXVARY.sh --domain=your.domain.com --upgrade-from=<installed-sha>
```

The installer will fail with a clear version-mismatch error if the installed
SHA does not match what `--upgrade-from` specifies, or if the flag is omitted.

## Post-install verification

After installation completes, open the printed HTTPS URL in a browser.
The setup wizard page should load. Complete the wizard, then sign in.

Verify the installed revision:
```bash
cat /etc/nexvary/installed_revision
```
Expected: `${COMMIT_SHA}`

Verify the services:
```bash
systemctl status nexvary-horizon nexvary-rtc nginx postgresql redis-server freeswitch
```

## Android APK

The matching debug APK is published as the `nexvary-cx-debug-apk` artifact
from the **NEXVARY CX Android — CI** workflow run on the same commit.

To pair the Android app:
1. Install the APK on your device
2. Sign in to the web admin panel
3. Navigate to **Settings → Pair Mobile App**
4. Scan the QR code with the app's Server tab → ربط عبر QR

## Checksums

Verify bundle integrity before installation:
```bash
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
```
